cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use KEO, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "KEO: a reproducible benchmark of k-means, e-means and o-means"
abstract: >-
  KEO compares k-means (Lloyd), e-means and o-means, three large-scale
  clustering algorithms, under one protocol, one set of metrics and one result
  store, and tests whether the headline claims of the e-means and o-means
  papers hold on a dataset neither paper evaluated (GloVe-100).
type: software
authors:
